1
00:00:03,871 --> 00:00:05,331
[MARY]
I'm not sure why,

2
00:00:05,373 --> 00:00:06,832
perhaps it was
the effect of living

3
00:00:06,874 --> 00:00:09,752
in the humdrum world of a
boarding school for so long.

4
00:00:09,793 --> 00:00:12,880
But I always wanted to
see the outside world.

5
00:00:12,922 --> 00:00:16,092
So I attended
university in Paris.

6
00:00:16,133 --> 00:00:19,262
While there, I discovered
a newfound sense of freedom

7
00:00:19,303 --> 00:00:21,722
I had never experienced.

8
00:00:22,639 --> 00:00:27,520
[MARY] And I also
discovered something else.

9
00:00:30,147 --> 00:00:32,858
[MARY] I became swept up
in the fervour around me,

10
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:34,693
without fully understanding it,

11
00:00:34,735 --> 00:00:36,153
and even participated in the

12
00:00:36,195 --> 00:00:39,449
university clubs'
student activism.

13
00:00:39,490 --> 00:00:43,869
I can't stress enough, the most
I did was distribute leaflets.

14
00:00:43,911 --> 00:00:44,787
However...

15
00:00:44,828 --> 00:00:46,497
[gun fires]

16
00:00:46,539 --> 00:00:48,499
[MARY]
...the group included radicals,

17
00:00:48,541 --> 00:00:52,628
and the officers were planning
to engage in subversive acts.

18
00:00:56,340 --> 00:00:58,259
[MARY]
Then, some days ago,

19
00:00:58,301 --> 00:01:00,010
I was visited out of the blue

20
00:01:00,052 --> 00:01:02,597
by a man calling
himself Milverton,

21
00:01:02,638 --> 00:01:04,181
saying that he had a register

22
00:01:04,223 --> 00:01:06,809
from the organisation
with my name on it.

23
00:01:06,850 --> 00:01:10,896
Now, wait! The Milverton?
Isn't he a newspaper tycoon?

24
00:01:10,938 --> 00:01:13,023
A man who runs
multiple media outlets

25
00:01:13,065 --> 00:01:15,276
has chosen to blackmail you.

26
00:01:15,318 --> 00:01:17,945
To what end? He's mad.

27
00:01:19,863 --> 00:01:22,658
[HOLMES]
I knew it.

28
00:01:22,699 --> 00:01:25,620
Charles Augustus Milverton,

29
00:01:25,661 --> 00:01:28,998
he lives up to his
second persona indeed.

30
00:01:30,040 --> 00:01:32,460
[HOLMES]
The King of Blackmailers.

31
00:01:32,502 --> 00:01:33,877
[HUDSON, WATSON gasp]

32
00:01:34,837 --> 00:01:36,880
[HOLMES]
Milverton is a disease.

33
00:01:36,922 --> 00:01:40,176
He derives pleasure from
watching others fall to ruin,

34
00:01:40,217 --> 00:01:43,887
and nothing else.
He revels in it.

35
00:01:43,929 --> 00:01:46,056
[WATSON] This doesn't
change a thing, really.

36
00:01:46,098 --> 00:01:49,644
I don't care whether or not
all of London knows.

37
00:01:49,685 --> 00:01:52,188
I won't back out
of our marriage.

38
00:01:52,229 --> 00:01:55,566
As for the French government,
they may not share your opinion.

39
00:01:55,608 --> 00:01:56,692
[WATSON grunts]

40
00:01:56,733 --> 00:01:58,444
She'll likely be extradited

41
00:01:58,486 --> 00:02:01,238
and thus, the two of you
will be separated.

42
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:04,325
Making married life
somewhat difficult.

43
00:02:04,367 --> 00:02:05,909
[WATSON gasps]

44
00:02:05,951 --> 00:02:08,579
[HUDSON] The treasure,
there's no way of recovering it?

45
00:02:08,621 --> 00:02:11,541
So it's impossible to meet
this blackmailer's demand.

46
00:02:11,582 --> 00:02:12,542
[knocking]

47
00:02:12,583 --> 00:02:14,001
[gasps]

48
00:02:20,466 --> 00:02:25,388
[HOLMES] Uncanny timing,
almost as if it were planned.

49
00:04:02,526 --> 00:04:05,696
How good of you to make the
trip all the way to my office,

50
00:04:05,738 --> 00:04:07,531
Mister Milverton.

51
00:04:07,573 --> 00:04:10,075
A meeting one might
say is long overdue,

52
00:04:10,117 --> 00:04:12,453
Mister Sherlock Holmes.

53
00:04:12,495 --> 00:04:15,623
Hm? And who is this gentleman?

54
00:04:15,665 --> 00:04:18,292
Doctor John H. Watson to you.

55
00:04:18,334 --> 00:04:19,502
Ah, I see!

56
00:04:19,543 --> 00:04:22,755
So that would make you
dear Miss Morstan's fiancé.

57
00:04:22,797 --> 00:04:26,216
This is quite the lovely
business we're in, isn't it?

58
00:04:26,258 --> 00:04:30,929
[WATSON] What're we discussing
here? The blasted weather?

59
00:04:30,971 --> 00:04:34,767
Moving on, I suspect you
know why I called on you.

60
00:04:34,809 --> 00:04:36,686
As an informed man,
I've received word

61
00:04:36,727 --> 00:04:40,105
the Treasure of Agra resides
at the bottom of the Thames.

62
00:04:40,147 --> 00:04:42,525
Before we discuss that,

63
00:04:42,566 --> 00:04:44,694
I'd like to confirm
Miss Morstan's name

64
00:04:44,735 --> 00:04:48,280
is on the group's
register as a formality.

65
00:04:48,322 --> 00:04:50,574
I assume you have it on you.

66
00:04:52,493 --> 00:04:54,077
[MILVERTON grunts]

67
00:05:05,088 --> 00:05:07,049
[MARY gasps]

68
00:05:07,090 --> 00:05:07,883
Mary!

69
00:05:07,924 --> 00:05:09,468
[HUDSON gasps]

70
00:05:09,510 --> 00:05:10,761
[MILVERTON chuckles]

71
00:05:10,803 --> 00:05:14,849
[cackling]

72
00:05:14,890 --> 00:05:17,518
[MILVERTON] I so do
love the follies of youth

73
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:20,688
and all the material
it ends up supplying me.

74
00:05:20,730 --> 00:05:22,398
Satisfied?

75
00:05:22,439 --> 00:05:25,442
Please, keep it.
That one is merely a copy.

76
00:05:25,484 --> 00:05:29,112
The actual register
is quite secure.

77
00:05:29,154 --> 00:05:31,948
Now then, returning
to the treasure.

78
00:05:31,990 --> 00:05:33,534
I haven't the
slightest intention

79
00:05:33,576 --> 00:05:36,412
of ceding an inch of ground.

80
00:05:36,453 --> 00:05:39,956
I will be staying at the
Langham until noon on Saturday.

81
00:05:39,998 --> 00:05:42,793
Do make the delivery
before I check out.

82
00:05:42,835 --> 00:05:44,420
I'm sure you'll
come up with some

83
00:05:44,461 --> 00:05:47,798
inventive way of
dredging the Thames.

84
00:05:47,840 --> 00:05:49,925
Good day, gentlemen.

85
00:05:56,807 --> 00:06:02,438
Damn him! That Milverton
is the devil himself!

86
00:06:02,479 --> 00:06:04,273
He mentioned that
the actual list

87
00:06:04,314 --> 00:06:06,609
was securely in his possession.

88
00:06:08,277 --> 00:06:10,028
[HOLMES]
Every time he stays in London,

89
00:06:10,070 --> 00:06:12,239
it's his practice to
rent out an entire floor

90
00:06:12,281 --> 00:06:14,241
at the Langham Hotel.

91
00:06:14,283 --> 00:06:16,076
But all blackmailers
tend to keep

92
00:06:16,118 --> 00:06:19,872
evidentiary material in the
safest place available to them.

93
00:06:19,914 --> 00:06:21,373
In Milverton's case,

94
00:06:21,415 --> 00:06:25,001
that would be his
oceanfront villa in Brighton.

95
00:06:26,002 --> 00:06:27,588
[HOLMES]
An eye for an eye.

96
00:06:27,630 --> 00:06:31,091
I'll sneak into his mansion
while he's still away.

97
00:06:31,133 --> 00:06:33,886
I insist on handling this,
so please, don't interfere.

98
00:06:33,928 --> 00:06:35,220
[HUDSON gasps]

99
00:06:35,262 --> 00:06:39,099
Let you handle everything?
Don't be ridiculous, Sherlock!

100
00:06:39,141 --> 00:06:40,434
I'm coming with you!

101
00:06:40,476 --> 00:06:42,519
We're going to see it
through, together!

102
00:06:42,561 --> 00:06:44,480
This entire matter
concerned Mary and I

103
00:06:44,521 --> 00:06:46,022
from the very beginning!

104
00:06:46,064 --> 00:06:48,567
[HOLMES stammers]

105
00:06:48,609 --> 00:06:50,903
After all, we are
partners, aren't we?!

106
00:06:50,945 --> 00:06:52,404
We stick side by side!

107
00:06:52,446 --> 00:06:55,365
Solving mysteries
or going to prison!

108
00:06:59,536 --> 00:07:02,748
Heh. Sharing a room
with you in jail, too?

109
00:07:02,790 --> 00:07:05,167
That should prove interesting.

110
00:07:05,208 --> 00:07:07,127
Sadly, I doubt that'll happen.

111
00:07:07,169 --> 00:07:09,463
[grunts]

112
00:07:09,505 --> 00:07:11,047
For you see, my friend,

113
00:07:11,089 --> 00:07:14,593
I, too, have a gift
when it comes to crime.

114
00:07:28,858 --> 00:07:30,275
Can't approach from the east.

115
00:07:30,317 --> 00:07:32,569
We would run the
risk of being spotted.

116
00:07:32,611 --> 00:07:36,490
Just to be safe, we should
head from the west.

117
00:07:36,532 --> 00:07:39,493
There's a flash of light,
first storey, west side.

118
00:07:39,535 --> 00:07:42,037
What? No one should be home.

119
00:07:42,078 --> 00:07:44,331
[gun firing]

120
00:07:44,373 --> 00:07:46,082
Gunfire!

121
00:07:46,124 --> 00:07:48,919
The devil? This
doesn't make sense.

122
00:07:48,961 --> 00:07:50,880
Sherlock, what now?

123
00:08:06,020 --> 00:08:08,981
[HOLMES]
So that's what this is about.

124
00:08:09,023 --> 00:08:11,984
[HOLMES] I've misread
the whole situation.

125
00:08:12,026 --> 00:08:14,236
[WATSON grunts]
How do you mean?

126
00:08:14,277 --> 00:08:16,822
John, head back
towards the town,

127
00:08:16,864 --> 00:08:18,615
once there, fetch the police.

128
00:08:18,657 --> 00:08:21,284
And what are you going to do?

129
00:08:21,326 --> 00:08:23,328
Stay here, observe.

130
00:08:23,370 --> 00:08:25,163
After you've
summoned the police,

131
00:08:25,205 --> 00:08:29,209
we'll retrieve the list
while they investigate.

132
00:08:29,251 --> 00:08:31,962
I'll do as you say
as long as you stay put.

133
00:08:32,004 --> 00:08:33,756
All right?

134
00:08:33,797 --> 00:08:36,550
Of course. Hurry along, now.

135
00:08:41,597 --> 00:08:43,265
[HOLMES]
Hmm.

136
00:08:51,732 --> 00:08:53,067
[gun firing]

137
00:08:53,108 --> 00:08:55,193
[HOLMES] They're having
a right proper shootout.

138
00:08:55,235 --> 00:08:58,072
Getting in through the ground
floor will be difficult.

139
00:09:06,371 --> 00:09:08,040
[HOLMES grunts]

140
00:09:11,460 --> 00:09:13,169
[grunts]

141
00:09:19,509 --> 00:09:22,638
[MILVERTON] I'm asking,
kindly lower your gun.

142
00:09:27,559 --> 00:09:30,270
[MILVERTON] Let's be
civilized and discuss this.

143
00:09:30,312 --> 00:09:32,188
Won't you hear me out?

144
00:09:32,230 --> 00:09:36,485
That's the least you can do.

145
00:09:36,526 --> 00:09:37,111
[HOLMES gasps]

146
00:09:37,152 --> 00:09:39,195
[floor creaks]

147
00:09:39,237 --> 00:09:41,031
[MILVERTON]
So, you've arrived,

148
00:09:41,073 --> 00:09:44,242
and right at the moment
I was expecting you.

149
00:09:46,369 --> 00:09:48,914
You've come just in time.
A second later,

150
00:09:48,956 --> 00:09:51,458
I would have had
a hole between my eyes.

151
00:09:51,500 --> 00:09:54,294
Welcome, Sherlock Holmes.

152
00:09:54,336 --> 00:09:57,380
Since neither of you clearly
understand the situation,

153
00:09:57,422 --> 00:10:00,425
allow me to explain it in full.

154
00:10:00,467 --> 00:10:03,345
[HOLMES]
That won't be necessary.

155
00:10:03,386 --> 00:10:06,348
Really, such a tortuously
roundabout way.

156
00:10:06,389 --> 00:10:09,059
How vexing.

157
00:10:09,101 --> 00:10:12,813
Blackmailing John's fiancée
was simply a means to an end.

158
00:10:12,855 --> 00:10:16,191
You wanted to drag me
into this affair.

159
00:10:16,232 --> 00:10:17,317
The treasure--

160
00:10:17,359 --> 00:10:19,695
it was an errand made to
drive us into a corner

161
00:10:19,736 --> 00:10:20,988
with no solution

162
00:10:21,030 --> 00:10:23,991
other than wresting the
evidence from your possession.

163
00:10:24,033 --> 00:10:26,535
Thus, why I'm here.

164
00:10:26,576 --> 00:10:30,914
[MILVERTON chuckles]
If I may make a confession,

165
00:10:30,956 --> 00:10:32,582
upon reading the report
that the Treasure

166
00:10:32,624 --> 00:10:35,085
was thrown into the river
just as I planned,

167
00:10:35,127 --> 00:10:37,546
I couldn't help but
laugh hysterically.

168
00:10:37,587 --> 00:10:39,131
Well, let's hear it.

169
00:10:39,173 --> 00:10:41,257
You used some similar
convoluted method

170
00:10:41,299 --> 00:10:43,593
to ensure he
showed up, no doubt.

171
00:10:43,635 --> 00:10:47,263
[MILVERTON] Astute, as always.
However, you can probably wager

172
00:10:47,305 --> 00:10:50,809
a fair guess why I
required your presence.

173
00:10:50,851 --> 00:10:55,480
You have a part
to play, detective.

174
00:10:55,522 --> 00:10:58,483
To arrest the man who
stands before you--

175
00:10:58,525 --> 00:11:00,777
Oh, how rude.

176
00:11:00,819 --> 00:11:03,697
May I present
the guest of honor.

177
00:11:03,739 --> 00:11:07,242
The British Empire's
greatest criminal mind...

178
00:11:07,283 --> 00:11:10,370
[thunder roars]

179
00:11:10,412 --> 00:11:12,998
[MILVERTON]
...the Lord of Crime.

180
00:11:24,134 --> 00:11:27,596
[MILVERTON] The Lord
of Crime, in the flesh,

181
00:11:27,637 --> 00:11:31,600
one Professor
William James Moriarty!

182
00:11:32,809 --> 00:11:36,855
Such a shame there are no
spectators to this comedy.

183
00:11:36,897 --> 00:11:42,611
The representatives of London's
duality: light and darkness.

184
00:11:42,652 --> 00:11:46,198
You couldn't ask
for a better show.

185
00:11:47,323 --> 00:11:49,826
[HARRY grunts]

186
00:11:49,868 --> 00:11:55,540
An immovable object meets an
unstoppable force. Eh, Louis?

187
00:11:55,582 --> 00:11:58,376
Right about now, I would
imagine your boss and mine

188
00:11:58,418 --> 00:12:00,295
ought to be in the thick of it,

189
00:12:00,336 --> 00:12:02,338
along with one other visitor.

190
00:12:02,380 --> 00:12:04,716
A standoff, between my employer,

191
00:12:04,758 --> 00:12:06,885
the professor,
and Sherlock Holmes.

192
00:12:06,927 --> 00:12:08,511
[LOUIS]
Holmes is here?

193
00:12:08,553 --> 00:12:11,014
[HARRY]
A bizarre drama is taking place,

194
00:12:11,056 --> 00:12:13,100
one I wished to see.

195
00:12:13,142 --> 00:12:16,145
Then again, we're
just the mercenaries.

196
00:12:16,186 --> 00:12:18,188
We're being paid
to slow you down.

197
00:12:18,230 --> 00:12:21,316
To buy enough time until
the performance concludes

198
00:12:21,357 --> 00:12:22,943
and the curtains draw.

199
00:12:22,985 --> 00:12:24,360
Heh.

200
00:12:24,402 --> 00:12:27,072
[LOUIS grunts]
Brother.

201
00:12:27,114 --> 00:12:29,658
[MILVERTON] Now then,
given the circumstances,

202
00:12:29,699 --> 00:12:32,535
events can only
play out one way.

203
00:12:32,577 --> 00:12:38,167
As follows, the detective
arrests the Lord of Crime.

204
00:12:39,084 --> 00:12:41,711
[MILVERTON] Moriarty,
if you choose to shoot me,

205
00:12:41,753 --> 00:12:44,464
I have made arrangements
for various media outlets

206
00:12:44,506 --> 00:12:47,884
to reveal your
identity to the public.

207
00:12:47,926 --> 00:12:51,096
However, if you are
willing to go along quietly,

208
00:12:51,138 --> 00:12:53,640
I guarantee you will live
the remainder of your life

209
00:12:53,682 --> 00:12:54,891
far from the spotlight.

210
00:12:54,933 --> 00:12:58,478
After handing you over to
the government, of course.

211
00:12:58,520 --> 00:13:00,856
You will be placed
under house arrest.

212
00:13:00,897 --> 00:13:03,192
Furthermore, all your
wants and needs,

213
00:13:03,233 --> 00:13:06,528
I guarantee they will
be taken care of.

214
00:13:06,569 --> 00:13:08,238
As for you, Holmes,

215
00:13:08,280 --> 00:13:10,866
unless you want your dear
friend's precious wedding

216
00:13:10,907 --> 00:13:15,453
to be cancelled, you will
submit and do as I say.

217
00:13:15,495 --> 00:13:17,831
But if you still have any
reason to doubt my word--

218
00:13:17,873 --> 00:13:22,002
[HOLMES] No, I know you
believe everything you said.

219
00:13:22,919 --> 00:13:24,713
If your only
objective was to create

220
00:13:24,754 --> 00:13:27,590
this drama and it all
plays out to a tee,

221
00:13:27,632 --> 00:13:28,884
I assume you will no longer

222
00:13:28,925 --> 00:13:32,554
have any reason to continue
blackmailing Miss Marston.

223
00:13:32,595 --> 00:13:36,599
That's right. Some commoner
girl with no news value?

224
00:13:36,641 --> 00:13:40,229
She meant nothing to me
from the start.

225
00:13:40,270 --> 00:13:42,731
This one, however...

226
00:13:42,772 --> 00:13:46,109
You're standing face-to-face
with a mass murderer,

227
00:13:46,151 --> 00:13:49,529
as if you would
allow him to slip away.

228
00:13:49,571 --> 00:13:53,909
Holmes! Arrest the
Lord of Crime. Do it!

229
00:13:57,537 --> 00:13:58,955
[MILVERTON chuckles]

230
00:13:58,997 --> 00:14:02,125
[MILVERTON] I'm in a position of
superiority over both of you,

231
00:14:02,167 --> 00:14:03,960
in every regard.

232
00:14:04,002 --> 00:14:08,257
You're pawns in a game you
never had a chance of winning.

233
00:14:08,298 --> 00:14:14,179
[MILVERTON cackling]

234
00:14:14,221 --> 00:14:14,846
Are you finished?

235
00:14:14,888 --> 00:14:17,099
[MILVERTON grunts, growls]

236
00:14:17,140 --> 00:14:19,851
[HOLMES]
My word, you ramble on.

237
00:14:20,852 --> 00:14:23,313
If you do consider
this a comedy,

238
00:14:23,355 --> 00:14:27,150
I'm sorry, but you aren't
the king; you're a jester.

239
00:14:27,192 --> 00:14:29,069
My dear fellow,

240
00:14:29,111 --> 00:14:32,322
you've misread the
situation entirely.

241
00:14:32,364 --> 00:14:34,950
And how's that?

242
00:14:34,991 --> 00:14:40,122
Come on, since he's here,
that's undoubtedly the case.

243
00:14:40,163 --> 00:14:42,874
Don't you agree with me, Liam?

244
00:14:42,916 --> 00:14:46,002
[HOLMES chuckles, laughing]

245
00:14:46,044 --> 00:14:47,796
Great to see you again!

246
00:14:47,837 --> 00:14:50,048
I'm glad it was you.

247
00:14:50,090 --> 00:14:53,135
To be honest, I couldn't bear
the thought if it wasn't.

248
00:14:53,176 --> 00:14:57,555
Finally, a worthy opponent.
No one else would do.

249
00:14:57,597 --> 00:14:58,974
Seeing you here...

250
00:14:59,015 --> 00:15:04,771
Well, to say it was a
relief is an understatement.

251
00:15:04,813 --> 00:15:06,440
[MILVERTON]
Wait.

252
00:15:06,481 --> 00:15:09,234
This-- This doesn't make sense!

253
00:15:09,276 --> 00:15:11,027
Why the casual banter?

254
00:15:11,069 --> 00:15:14,114
Don't tell me...
Holmes and Moriarty...

255
00:15:14,156 --> 00:15:15,490
It can't be!

256
00:15:15,531 --> 00:15:18,785
If the two of them had been in
contact, I would have known!

257
00:15:18,827 --> 00:15:21,537
A detective and
an arch criminal?

258
00:15:21,579 --> 00:15:24,499
"Liam"? What the devil
are you talking about?

259
00:15:24,540 --> 00:15:28,170
I demand you answer me,
Sherlock Holmes!

260
00:15:28,211 --> 00:15:33,049
Liam, the only thing I want is
to rescue my partner's marriage.

261
00:15:33,091 --> 00:15:36,470
I'm fine with
whatever becomes of me.

262
00:15:36,511 --> 00:15:38,930
So what about you?

263
00:15:38,972 --> 00:15:42,142
Do you care if he reveals
your name to the world?

264
00:15:46,480 --> 00:15:47,814
[MILVERTON gasps]

265
00:15:47,856 --> 00:15:52,319
Hardly, since that was
always my intention.

266
00:15:52,361 --> 00:15:55,613
Then we've reached our decision.

267
00:15:55,655 --> 00:15:58,408
Wait a minute!
You can't kill me!

268
00:15:58,450 --> 00:16:01,619
I-- The evidence!
I'll make it public!

269
00:16:01,661 --> 00:16:03,621
[HOLMES]
No, you won't.

270
00:16:03,663 --> 00:16:04,998
You may have the evidence,

271
00:16:05,040 --> 00:16:07,959
but you haven't arranged
for it to be published.

272
00:16:08,001 --> 00:16:11,296
You said yourself that
Mary had no news value,

273
00:16:11,338 --> 00:16:12,255
don't you remember?

274
00:16:12,297 --> 00:16:14,549
[grunts]

275
00:16:14,590 --> 00:16:18,636
I thought as much. Whenever
someone sees right through you,

276
00:16:18,678 --> 00:16:21,597
you're prone to
clenching your back teeth.

277
00:16:21,639 --> 00:16:23,766
Yes, like that.

278
00:16:23,808 --> 00:16:25,685
Hold on!

279
00:16:25,727 --> 00:16:28,730
[MILVERTON]
This is impossible.

280
00:16:28,771 --> 00:16:31,358
Choosing to be so irrational.

281
00:16:31,400 --> 00:16:34,777
One I could understand,
but both of them?

282
00:16:42,118 --> 00:16:44,037
[MILVERTON grunts]

283
00:16:56,966 --> 00:16:58,968
[MILVERTON gasps, grunts]

284
00:17:00,387 --> 00:17:04,682
[HOLMES] Your exit's not
your choice--it's mine.

285
00:17:17,571 --> 00:17:19,781
- -[clang]
- -[HARRY grunts]

286
00:17:19,822 --> 00:17:21,657
[BOTH gasp]

287
00:17:38,300 --> 00:17:40,051
[HOLMES]
After all this,

288
00:17:40,093 --> 00:17:43,679
I still can't definitively prove
you're the Lord of Crime.

289
00:17:45,307 --> 00:17:47,100
[HOLMES] Meanwhile,
you've made me a hero

290
00:17:47,142 --> 00:17:50,520
who exposed the misdeeds
of the nobility.

291
00:17:50,562 --> 00:17:52,397
I was always
a step behind you.

292
00:17:52,439 --> 00:17:55,691
Trapped, dancing in
the palm of your hand.

293
00:18:01,197 --> 00:18:02,740
[HOLMES]
Still, though...

294
00:18:06,453 --> 00:18:07,579
It's not as though that means

295
00:18:07,621 --> 00:18:10,665
I'm completely
devoid of free will.

296
00:18:10,706 --> 00:18:13,751
You never expected me
to kill Milverton.

297
00:18:15,295 --> 00:18:19,257
[HOLMES] Don't assume everyone
will conform to your whims.

298
00:18:19,299 --> 00:18:21,593
Least of all, me.

299
00:18:23,178 --> 00:18:26,515
The game's afoot, and
there's no going back, Liam!

300
00:18:26,556 --> 00:18:29,267
I swear I will unravel
your tangled web

301
00:18:29,309 --> 00:18:32,312
and apprehend you my own way.

302
00:18:35,064 --> 00:18:36,399
[WILLIAM chuckles]

303
00:18:36,441 --> 00:18:38,943
[WILLIAM] And my
response to that challenge

304
00:18:38,985 --> 00:18:41,696
is the same as before.

305
00:18:41,737 --> 00:18:45,950
"Come and catch me if you can,
Sherlock Holmes."

306
00:18:50,664 --> 00:18:54,543
Yes. I'll see you soon.

307
00:19:03,510 --> 00:19:05,303
My patron got himself killed.

308
00:19:05,345 --> 00:19:07,805
Was only a matter
of time, I suppose.

309
00:19:07,847 --> 00:19:10,392
No reason to be
on the clock anymore.

310
00:19:10,433 --> 00:19:11,976
[HARRY whistles]

311
00:19:12,018 --> 00:19:13,228
[RUSKIN grunts]

312
00:19:13,269 --> 00:19:14,479
[GOSLING grunts]

313
00:19:14,521 --> 00:19:15,855
The show's over.

314
00:19:15,897 --> 00:19:19,484
Hopefully, I'll never have to
cross paths with you again.

315
00:19:19,526 --> 00:19:20,818
[door slams]

316
00:19:20,860 --> 00:19:22,862
[LOUIS]
If Milverton is dead,

317
00:19:22,904 --> 00:19:25,657
then where are
Holmes and William?

318
00:19:33,873 --> 00:19:36,751
It was a true privilege, sir.

319
00:19:44,593 --> 00:19:46,595
[WATSON gasps]
The villa!

320
00:19:46,636 --> 00:19:48,221
Uh!

321
00:19:49,723 --> 00:19:51,600
[WATSON]
Sherlock!

322
00:19:51,641 --> 00:19:52,350
Are you...?

323
00:19:52,392 --> 00:19:56,020
Yes. I'm fine. Thanks, though.

324
00:19:57,439 --> 00:20:01,317
he evidence against
Mary is gone; she's free.

325
00:20:01,359 --> 00:20:03,027
[gasps]

326
00:20:03,069 --> 00:20:05,988
[POLICEMAN 22A] Mister Holmes!
What is the meaning of all this?

327
00:20:06,030 --> 00:20:09,075
Please explain yourself at once.

328
00:20:09,117 --> 00:20:11,244
Very well.

329
00:20:11,286 --> 00:20:16,458
There'll be a lot of paperwork,
but here is the short version.

330
00:20:17,959 --> 00:20:21,546
[HOLMES] This is the gun
I used to kill Milverton.

331
00:20:21,588 --> 00:20:23,089
You may arrest me now.

332
00:20:23,131 --> 00:20:24,132
[POLICE gasp]

333
00:20:24,173 --> 00:20:26,968
What?! You killed him?

334
00:20:27,009 --> 00:20:30,054
John, the wedding--

335
00:20:30,096 --> 00:20:33,057
I'm sorry, I don't think
I'll be able to attend.

336
00:20:33,099 --> 00:20:34,225
[WATSON gasps]

337
00:20:34,267 --> 00:20:36,185
[POLICEMAN 22A]
We have no choice. Take him in!

338
00:20:36,227 --> 00:20:37,812
[POLICE]
Sir!

339
00:20:40,940 --> 00:20:44,402
[whimpers]

340
00:20:44,444 --> 00:20:46,279
[WATSON]
You promised me.

341
00:20:46,321 --> 00:20:49,449
I thought we were
partners until the end!

342
00:20:50,825 --> 00:20:54,036
[WATSON]
Sherlock!

343
00:21:03,296 --> 00:21:06,132
Although we're rid
of that pest, Milverton,

344
00:21:06,174 --> 00:21:08,092
Holmes was unfortunately the one

345
00:21:08,134 --> 00:21:10,261
that ended up
pulling the trigger.

346
00:21:10,303 --> 00:21:13,348
You aren't to blame
for this, Brother.

347
00:21:13,389 --> 00:21:15,266
There's no question he
had his own motivations

348
00:21:15,308 --> 00:21:17,393
for shooting that man.

349
00:21:18,603 --> 00:21:22,565
[WILLIAM]
I have a confession, Louis.

350
00:21:22,607 --> 00:21:25,735
I never meant to let him become
a murderer as soon as this.

351
00:21:25,777 --> 00:21:27,362
[gasps]

352
00:21:27,403 --> 00:21:29,280
[WILLIAM]
I thought that for him,

353
00:21:29,322 --> 00:21:30,448
killing another would be

354
00:21:30,490 --> 00:21:33,326
the most difficult
hurdle to overcome.

355
00:21:36,996 --> 00:21:39,708
[WILLIAM]
But once you kill one person,

356
00:21:39,749 --> 00:21:42,502
murdering another
makes no difference.

357
00:21:42,544 --> 00:21:44,462
Meaning,

358
00:21:44,504 --> 00:21:47,632
that in all likelihood,
he'll hunt me down,

359
00:21:47,674 --> 00:21:49,759
and when he does...

360
00:21:49,801 --> 00:21:52,928
...he'll aim to end my life.

361
00:23:32,403 --> 00:23:34,989
[HOLMES] Next time on
Moriarty the Patriot  :

362
00:23:35,030 --> 00:23:38,117
"The Final Problem, Act One."
